    "es22TaskDeletion": {
      "source": "tests/fixtures/stream_ac5000/es22_task_delete_masked.json",
      "upstreamSource": "issue #234, exports A (during the app writes) and B (fresh session after a config entry reload)",
      "sourceBlobSha": "3986a39ae28b2c69c9e2105b1a1724208ea31075",
      "note": "Seven frames from the two diagnostics downloads @slaapyhoofd attached to issue #234 on 2026-09-03, taken while he added a charge task beside an existing discharge task and then deleted the discharge one. They are the evidence that an `f40` container carries the whole task list rather than a delta: after the deletion every later readback carries the survivor alone, and no frame ever carried the deleted task by itself. Timestamps are UTC; his own clock runs two hours ahead. Both downloads were already masked before upload, so the only identifier-shaped run in any payload is the filler. The frames are a list so the repository-wide fixture sweep in tests/test_frame_capture.py reaches them; each carries its role as a field. Every frame was passed through the integration's own masking before being stored here, so the fixture is masked by the code under test rather than by hand. The masking reaches every identifier in these frames by shape alone: the twelve character lower case hex run that once had to be named is covered by the pass anchored on the serial it is joined to, and all seven frames here are reproduced byte for byte from the raw downloads with no caller naming anything.",
